class_name TutorialData
extends RefCounted
## Text for the How To Play screen and the first-run context tips. Every number here mirrors the game code
## (player.gd S table, weapons.gd LIST, enemies.gd TYPES, lighting.gd, objects.gd / loot.gd) - keep them in sync.
##
## Templates use {action} tokens that GameInput.fill() replaces with the key / button / touch wording of the
## ACTIVE control scheme ({move} {aim} {attack} {sprint} {bomb} {weapon_next} {weapon_prev} {headlamp} {battery}
## {use_water} {use_bandage} {use_food} {tactical_map} {status_hud} {run_stats} {pause} ...).
## Line prefixes: "## " sub-heading, "- " bullet, "[kb] " / "[pad] " / "[touch] " = only for that scheme.

const PAGES := [
